{
  "_about": "Reviewed analyte registry for lab unit harmonization. Each entry: keywords (matched against lowercased column name + description, longest match wins), exclude (disambiguation), conventional_unit (US), min/max (physiologic plausibility bounds in the conventional unit; intentionally generous to admit diseased values), alt_factors (multipliers that turn an alternative-unit value into the conventional unit; applied only when the raw value is out of range and the product lands in range). Factors are derived from molar mass / SI prefixes per NIST SP 811 and UCUM. This file holds no dataset rows, assignments, or expected outputs; tune bounds/factors per analyte during revision.",
  "_references": [
    "https://www.nist.gov/pml/special-publication-811/nist-guide-si-chapter-8",
